// R16 carrier: Fetch adapter failure-surface parity against the HTTP/1.1 reference
// (PLAN/r16-fetch-failure-surface-parity-*). Derived from the R15 H1/H2 carrier: same
// wires, observation schema, ledger and coherence checks; rows are the DEC166 registry
// with the H1 reference row that ran on the same runtime.
// Every row observes the COMPLETE public surface (error identity, response
// identity, delivered body/file identity, full hook tuple, hook payloads,
// normalized event order, exactly-one public error, wire hits and
// connections) and compares it to the signature frozen per runtime below;
// any drift is a ledger failure. One static parity check runs at load over
// the frozen tables: the node and bun tables must agree on every parity
// field except the sanctioned RUNTIME_SPLIT (the documented residuals, never
// silent allowances). There are no per-row protocol pairs (DEC166): the H1
// rows are live references on the same runtime, not pair partners.
// Identity-only fields (message, causeMessage/causeName/causeCode/
// causeDescriptor, responseHeaderNames/Values, closeEmitted, progressEmitted,
// fixtureEchoes) are pinned exactly per runtime but are NOT parity claims.
// No zstd import: the truncated frame is rebuilt byte-for-byte by the
// RFC 8878 raw-block writer.

const RUNTIME: 'node' | 'bun' = typeof process.versions.bun === 'string' ? 'bun' : 'node';
